# Context discipline (ALWAYS ON)

Pinky rules stay **always on** until the user opts out. Skills are **available** by default — but do **not** load everything into context.

## Do

- Read / open **only** files needed for **this** user prompt.
- For skills: load **one** matching `SKILL.md` (and its companions only if that skill says so). Never bulk-read all of `skills/`.
- Prefer search/grep over opening whole trees.
- Keep replies Caveman-short so tokens stay low.

## Don't

- Don't preload every Pinky skill, format doc, or rule file "just in case".
- Don't dump `ADR-FORMAT.md` / `CONTEXT-FORMAT.md` unless running `/grill-with-docs`.
- Don't attach the whole kit README/INSTALL into every turn after install.

## Opt out

User says "stop caveman", "normal mode", "don't use pinky", "disable [skill/rule]" → stop that layer for the session (or until they re-enable).
